# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ted AI — .gitignore
# NOTE: gitignore does NOT support inline comments — a pattern with a trailing
# "# comment" matches nothing. Keep every comment on its own line.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# === SECRETS — never commit these ===
# real API keys live in config.py; commit config.example.py instead
config.py
.env
*.env
# Spotify OAuth token
data/.spotify_cache
# email credentials (also lives in ~ — here for safety)
.ted_email_config.json

# === Python ===
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# === Large model files (download separately, don't commit) ===
data/kokoro-v1.0.onnx
data/voices-v1.0.bin

# === Generated / runtime data ===
# Everything in data/ is generated, downloaded, or personal — models, the
# SQLite memory, OAuth caches, logs. Ignore the whole directory and opt files
# back IN, rather than listing them one by one: the old approach meant every
# new runtime file (SQLite's -wal/-shm sidecars, the launcher log) defaulted to
# being committed, and the WAL sidecar carries the same private content as
# memory.db itself.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
ted_errors.log
ted_errors.log.*

# === Build artifacts (rebuild, don't commit) ===
# macOS app bundle — rebuild with tools/make_app.sh
Ted.app/

# === Build artifacts ===
# compiled Swift binary (build with native/build.sh)
native/ted_audio
native/ted_control
*.o

# === Editor / OS cruft ===
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
# FUSE leftovers from mounted-folder tooling (deleted-but-open file stubs)
.fuse_hidden*
**/.fuse_hidden*
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# === User inbox contents (documents you drop in to index) ===
inbox/*
!inbox/.gitkeep
ted_map.html

# === holding pen for files on their way out ===
# device_bash cannot delete, so removals land here first. Never source.
_to_delete/

# === test scratch ===
# test_codebase.py writes a probe into docs/ and removes it. A run that dies
# before the cleanup leaves these behind, and the NEXT run then fails on them.
docs/_ted_write_test.md
docs/_ted_write_test.md.ted-backup
